WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.970
If I create an AWS account, will my bill surprise me?

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.970
That's the question in this mission.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.530
It takes about an hour and costs nothing.

4
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.570
And you can do the first three steps without an account.

5
00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:15.563
Before opening any tool, open a file and write this down.

6
00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:18.543
What do you think costs the most in a small account?

7
00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:21.863
You can be wrong. Being wrong is what makes a good article.

8
00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:24.513
Now download the sample cost file.

9
00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:26.173
The data is fictional.

10
00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:29.543
Paste it into your AI assistant with this request.

11
00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:30.873
Notice the last item:

12
00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:32.273
don't give me the conclusion.

13
00:00:32.273 --> 00:00:34.883
You want questions, not an answer to copy.

14
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:37.227
Now check the math without AI,

15
00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:38.967
using this command.

16
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:43.977
The total went from 0.92 USD to 25.63 USD.

17
00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:46.137
And look at the first line of the list.

18
00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:48.687
The biggest increase is the NAT Gateway,

19
00:00:48.687 --> 00:00:52.857
at 16.20 USD. It's not the EC2 server.

20
00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:56.193
Now compare. Do the AI's totals match?

21
00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:58.513
Did it notice that the biggest increase is the NAT

22
00:00:58.513 --> 00:01:01.793
Gateway? Did it state a price that wasn't in the file?

23
00:01:01.793 --> 00:01:04.773
If so, ask for the source and open the link.

24
00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:06.033
Write it all down.

25
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.163
What didn't match is your best evidence.

26
00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:10.253
If you already have an account,

27
00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:11.963
create a spending alert.

28
00:01:12.173 --> 00:01:15.413
The commands are in the mission and run in CloudShell,

29
00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:17.843
the terminal that comes in your browser.

30
00:01:18.073 --> 00:01:19.923
At the end, you check it like this.

31
00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:24.753
It warns you when actual spending passes 80% of US$ 5.

32
00:01:24.753 --> 00:01:27.823
And when the forecast passes US$ 5.

33
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.550
And here's the part that confuses people most.

34
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.750
The alert warns you, but it doesn't block anything.

35
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.010
It doesn't turn anything off by itself.

36
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.190
If an email arrives, it's up to you.

37
00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.820
I recommend keeping this alert,

38
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.730
because it's free and protects the account.

39
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.450
The command to delete it is also in the mission.

40
00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:48.643
That's it, you already have an article in your hands.

41
00:01:48.993 --> 00:01:51.763
The topic is how to avoid billing surprises.

42
00:01:51.973 --> 00:01:53.343
The evidence is yours:

43
00:01:53.553 --> 00:01:55.593
the hypothesis, the AI's answer,

44
00:01:55.593 --> 00:01:57.803
the command output and what didn't match.

45
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.383
Write it in your own words.

46
00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:00.903
AI only reviews.

47
00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.267
One note before we finish.

48
00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.867
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned

49
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:07.907
voice, with my authorization.

50
00:02:07.907 --> 00:02:09.887
And this is an independent project.

51
00:02:09.887 --> 00:02:12.757
It is not official AWS material.
